# CyberLab — environment variables (template)
#
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in YOUR OWN values locally:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Rules:
# - The real ".env" file must NEVER be committed to Git. It is listed in
#   .gitignore on purpose; a committed API key is a leaked API key.
# - This template contains variable NAMES ONLY, with empty placeholders.
#   It is safe to commit, and it is the only env file that belongs in the
#   repository.
# - In production, the Cloudflare Worker does not read a local file. The
#   same values are set as Worker secrets in the Cloudflare Dashboard
#   (Worker -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets). See SETUP.md, Step 7.
# - For local Worker development, "wrangler dev" reads ".dev.vars"
#   (also git-ignored) — you can copy the same values into that file.

# Brevo API key — used by the Worker (as env.BREVO_API_KEY) to send
# password-reset code emails. Get yours from Brevo:
# Settings -> SMTP & API -> API Keys. Required for the forgot-password
# flow; without it that endpoint returns an honest 503 and the rest of
# the app works normally.
BREVO_API_KEY=

# (Optional) Verified Brevo sender email, read by the Worker as
# env.BREVO_FROM. Leave empty to use the Worker's built-in default sender.
BREVO_FROM=

# (Optional) Extra pepper for session-token storage hashing, read by the
# Worker as env.SESSION_PEPPER. Any long random string you choose; the
# API works without it.
SESSION_PEPPER=
